y fast-path heartbeats do not. Failed pipeline returns to ordinary retries, whose missing leader logs cause snapshot fallback.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-replication\",\n        \"B-append\",\n        \"B-apply-queue\",\n        \"B-snapshot\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-quorum\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-dispatch\",\n        \"M-replicate\",\n        \"M-consume\",\n        \"M-append\",\n        \"M-fsm\",\n        \"M-heartbeat\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Heartbeat expiry permits configured voters to campaign. Pre-vote does not advance term; actual election persists term and self-vote, asks each other latest voter once and tallies a per-campaign channel. Vote handlers reject ineligible candidates and stale histories, and persist a new vote before granting. Newer terms, voter lease loss or removal cause authority loss; tenure exit resolves pending leader futures and stops workers. Transfer waits for selected replication catch-up then TimeoutNow triggers a privileged election. Snapshot installation and restart reconstruct history/configuration; explicit user restore aborts pending writes and creates a new snapshot-backed boundary.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-vote\",\n        \"B-leader\",\n        \"B-reconstruct\",\n        \"B-snapshot\",\n        \"B-membership\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-last-position\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-election\",\n        \"M-vote\",\n        \"M-leader\",\n        \"M-start\",\n        \"M-elect-producer\",\n        \"M-lease\",\n        \"M-transfer\",\n        \"M-install\",\n        \"M-user-restore\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Voting log freshness links future authority to retained history; new tenure commitment starts empty and requires a current-term entry before inherited prefix can commit. Old replication workers retain old tracker and stepDown channels; old election replies retain old campaign channels. Latest voter membership controls election and commitment, changes are gated by prior configuration/current-term commitment, and suffix truncation can revert pending membership. Snapshot metadata records committed membership and restore/restart rebuild context. Client leader loss is uncertain completion, distinct from completed FSM application. Verification is another authority consumer: its voter-count threshold is fed by all registered peer callbacks, an unresolved eligibility discrepancy.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-leader\",\n        \"B-vote\",\n        \"B-commit\",\n        \"B-reconstruct\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-verify-register\",\n        \"B-verify-confirm\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-last-position\",\n        \"F-quorum\",\n        \"F-verify-tally\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-leader\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-vote\",\n        \"M-dispatch\",\n        \"M-start\",\n        \"M-elect-producer\",\n        \"M-membership\",\n        \"M-api-apply\",\n        \"M-verify-register\",\n        \"M-verify-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"VerifyLeader nonvoter callback eligibility is the principal selected discriminator.\",\n      \"Transient failed append after successful truncation: recovery before restart/snapshot remains unresolved; existing injected-error test covers nonconflicting appends.\",\n      \"Split vote persistence failure history and old snapshot boundary behavior remain sourced open surfaces.\",\n      \"Transport pipeline error correspondence and deeper transfer overlap paths remain unread.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and authority paths and their history, membership, recovery and completion dependencies are now traced; local discrepancies remain 